<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Vogels lifts H1 shr but div falls.</title>
<headline>Vogels lifts H1 shr but div falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     59	  vs 55</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 25	  vs 35</p>
<p>    After tax profit	10.83     vs 10.16</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   10.92     vs 10.15</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.09 paid vs 0.01 received</p>
<p>    Revenue		   11.61     vs 10.74</p>
<p>    Expenditure	     0.69	vs 0.59</p>
<p>Div payable Feb 26</p>
<p>on register Feb 7</p>
<p>Full name: Vogelstruisbult Metal Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE: Directors said profit after tax was expected to be lower in the second six months as the two largest contributors to the group's investment income, Gold Fields Coal Ltd and Zincor, generally declared a larger proportion of their dividends which accrue to the group in the December period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
